## Purpose

Return the MFRP-P3 provider-free historical replay: a frozen fixture corpus
binding 20 cases across all 18 roadmap replay families and all 7 zero-tolerance
classes to the seven pinned historical sources, a deterministic read-only
replay helper, focused tests, the pre-replay frozen ledger, and this return.
This return reports mechanical replay evidence only; it selects at most
`REPLAY_PASS_CANDIDATE` and leaves `REPLAY_PASS` to the reviewer.

## Target / Source

Target: the exact five-path P3 manifest named in the work order's Required
Artifact Manifest.

Source authority: the canonical work order above and its paired baseline
`docs/baselines/CVF_GC018_MFRP_P3_HISTORICAL_REPLAY_AND_FROZEN_DEFECT_LEDGER_2026-09-01.md`.
The seven frozen historical sources are listed in the ledger's Source
Verification Block with independently recomputed SHA-256 values, all
`MATCH`.

## Scope / Methodology

1. Captured `executionBaseHead` via `git rev-parse HEAD` and confirmed a clean
   worktree before any authoring.
2. Confirmed material dispatch commit `57e51e8a86d44ee8602ade8af7dfff39eab87499`
   is an ancestor of `executionBaseHead`.
3. Read `AGENTS.md`, the session bootstrap read model, active handoff, guard
   orientation index, literal-format gotchas reference, the canonical work
   order, the paired baseline, the P2 accepted worker return, both P2 helper
   sources, and all seven frozen historical sources.
4. Independently recomputed all seven frozen historical source SHA-256 values
   before authoring the fixture; all seven matched the work order's Frozen
   Historical Source Set table exactly.
5. Confirmed all five authorized output paths were absent at the clean
   execution base.
6. Ran the pre-implementation autorun gate at the clean execution base:
   83/83 commands PASS.
7. Authored the fixture corpus and the pre-replay ledger together, then froze
   both before running the replay helper for the first time.
8. Ran the replay helper once (first run); it reported `RETURN_TO_DESIGN`
   because case `MFRP-P3-C11`'s frozen expectation (a `NONE`-class case whose
   expected receipt result is a conservative-surfaced gap, not a bare clean
   pass) exposed a defect in the helper's own evaluation contract, which at
   that point treated every `NONE`-class case as required to resolve to a
   silently clean result.
9. Diagnosed the defect as a helper-code modeling gap, not a frozen-fixture
   or frozen-ledger defect: the roadmap does not require every non-zero-
   tolerance family to be silently clean, and `MFRP-P3-C11` correctly and
   honestly encodes GCLH-RV-3's documented byte-domain residual finding.
   Repaired only the helper's `_evaluate_case` function so a `NONE`-class
   case is accepted when its expectation is either a recognized clean result
   or a recognized conservative-surface result. Neither the fixture nor the
   ledger was edited at any point after the freeze.
10. Ran the replay helper again (final run): `REPLAY_PASS_CANDIDATE`, zero
    source drift, zero false negatives, zero false positives, 100% recall in
    every zero-tolerance class.
11. Wrote the focused test suite; two test-only defects surfaced on first run
    (a cross-drive `relative_to` crash under an out-of-repo tmp fixture path,
    and a vacuous substring assertion that matched the module's own
    docstring prose). Repaired both in the helper/test files only; reran to
    32/32 passing, then reran the frozen fixture replay again unchanged.
12. Ran the P2 focused regression suites to confirm no P2 production surface
    was touched: 18/18 passing.
13. Ran `run_worker_return_fast_gate.py`; it initially reported five
    violations, all located in the ledger's missing administrative sections
    (Checker Source Read-Ahead Block, Agent Operation Trace Block, Epistemic
    Process Block) and the two new Python paths' missing Core Guard
    authorization. Added exactly those administrative sections to the
    ledger without altering its Freeze Record, Source Verification Block, or
    reconciliation tables, then repaired one literal-format self-trigger
    (quoting the real `Agent Operation Trace Block` heading inside backticks
    elsewhere in the same document, matching literal-format gotcha 5) and one
    unparseable path-list field in that same trace block. Full trace: see
    Ledger Post-Freeze Administrative Addition Disclosure below.
14. Reran the full worker-return fast gate to a clean pass.

