## Finding-To-Governance Learning Disposition

REVIEWER_CORRECTED_EXISTING_OWNER_ABSORPTION: the first replay run exposed
that the helper's own evaluation contract incorrectly required every
non-zero-tolerance (`NONE`-class) case to resolve to a silently clean result,
which would have made it impossible to honestly represent a real,
correctly-surfaced non-zero-tolerance finding (GCLH-RV-3's byte-domain
residual) without either mislabeling it or omitting it. The finding is
absorbed into `_evaluate_case`'s `NONE`-class branch and the focused
regression suite; no new governance owner or separate rule family is needed.
Any future P4 canary design remains a separate operator-checkpoint tranche.

## Epistemic Process Block

### Expected Result / Prediction

The frozen fixture, bound to seven real accepted CVF historical sources,
should reproduce 100% zero-tolerance recall under a correctly-specified
conservative local envelope, with zero source drift and zero unexplained
divergence between first-run and final-run evidence beyond a disclosed
code-only repair.

### Evidence Comparison

First run: `RETURN_TO_DESIGN`, one false positive (`MFRP-P3-C11`), zero false
negatives, zero source drift. Final run after the disclosed
`_evaluate_case` repair: `REPLAY_PASS_CANDIDATE`, zero false positives, zero
false negatives, zero source drift, 100% recall in all seven zero-tolerance
classes. The fixture's corpus SHA-256 and the ledger's Freeze Record content
are identical across both runs, independently reconfirmed by direct
rehashing after the repair.

### Contradiction Or Gap Disposition

The one first-run divergence (`MFRP-P3-C11`) is fully explained by the
disclosed helper-code defect, not by a frozen-fixture or frozen-ledger error,
a source hash mismatch, or a hidden zero-tolerance miss. No other
contradiction, hidden gap, or unrepresentable conservative route was
observed.

### Claim Update

Evidence supports `REPLAY_PASS_CANDIDATE` only. The reviewer independently
recomputes all identities and reruns the replay and P2 regressions before
selecting `REPLAY_PASS` or `RETURN_TO_DESIGN`.

