## Worker Experience Retrospective

The first replay run's `RETURN_TO_DESIGN` initially looked like a frozen-
fixture defect, which would have forced a `RETURN_TO_DESIGN` disposition for
this whole tranche since the work order forbids any post-freeze fixture edit.
Closer inspection showed the fixture's case content was correct and honest
(a real GCLH-RV-3 residual, clearly labeled `HISTORICAL_OUTCOME` and
`zeroToleranceClass: NONE`); the defect was in the helper's overly strict
`NONE`-class evaluation contract, which is ordinary implementation code, not
frozen evidence. Distinguishing "the frozen fixture is wrong" from "the code
that reads the frozen fixture is wrong" was the deciding factor in choosing a
code-only repair over `RETURN_TO_DESIGN`. Separately, the worker-return fast
gate's requirement that every changed `docs/reviews/` artifact carry the full
administrative section set applied even to an already-frozen ledger; adding
those sections without touching the ledger's Freeze Record required treating
"frozen" as scoped to the evidentiary content (corpus hash, case-set digest,
expected outcomes) rather than to the entire file, and disclosing that
judgment call explicitly for reviewer scrutiny rather than silently editing
around it.

